  "notes": [
   "The page's own title heading is cut off from the text; section_heading uses the award name as printed in the body ('Associate in Arts in Social Justice Studies for Transfer').",
   "Foothill is on the quarter system: 'Major: 28-33' is recorded as total_units, the printed 90-unit minimum for this award as degree_total, and Cal-GETC (45 units) as ge_units; transferable electives fill the rest of the 90 units with no units printed.",
   "Students choose one of three emphases (option_group 'Emphasis'). Printed option totals: Option 1 28-33, Option 2 28-32, Option 3 28-33.",
   "List A in each option is printed in five areas (1 History or Government, 2 Arts and Humanities, 3 Social Science, 4 Quantitative Reasoning and Research Methods, 5 Major Preparation); the rule is four courses from at least three areas. Each List A block lists every course once in catalog order; courses printed in both Area 3 and Area 5 (ANTH 2A, COMM 12, ECON 25) and POLI 15 (Areas 1 and 5) appear once.",
   "ECON 25H is printed as an alternative to ECON 25 only in Area 5 (and the Option 1 core choice), not in Area 3; it is recorded as an alternative on the single ECON 25 entry. POLI 15H is printed only in Area 1 and the Option 1 core list.",
   "Footnote 1: courses so marked (e.g., ANTH 2A, COMM 12, ECON 25, ETHN 1, POLI 15, SOC 1) may be completed only once for credit to satisfy either the core or the support requirement.",
   "Units are not printed beside the choice-list and List A courses, so their units are null; only the core courses show 4 units.",
   "Catalog codes (e.g., ANTH 2A, HIST 17A, SOC 1H) match the closed list's zero-padded codes (ANTH 002A, HIST 017A, SOC 001H), so none is marked as a catalog addition.",
   "The single Program Learning Outcomes list is printed for the program and shared by all three emphases."
